{
  "findings": [
    {
      "location": "html，引用罗马书7:18的段落",
      "severity": "major",
      "source_quote": "…that in me (that is, in my flesh,) dwelleth no good thing…. …for to will is present with me; but how to perform that which is good I find not",
      "suggested_fix": "将两处引文分别改为<em>……在我里面（就是在我肉体之中），没有良善……</em>和<em>……因为我有行善的意愿，却不知道如何行出善来——罗马书 7:18。</em>。",
      "translation_quote": "……在我（就是在我肉体里）没有良善可居……；……因为立志为善在我，我却得不出来行那美善"
    },
    {
      "location": "html，彼得第一次回答耶稣的段落",
      "severity": "major",
      "source_quote": "Jesus said, “Feed my lambs.”",
      "suggested_fix": "将此处“喂养我的羊。”改为“喂养我的小羊。”，保留后文“牧养我的羊”的区别。",
      "translation_quote": "耶稣说，“喂养我的羊。”"
    },
    {
      "location": "html，回忆该亚法家的段落",
      "severity": "major",
      "source_quote": "He saw Jesus being brutally handled, falsely accused, and spat upon.",
      "suggested_fix": "将“并被人唾弃”改为“并被人吐唾沫”。",
      "translation_quote": "他看见耶稣被粗暴对待，遭受虚假的指控，并被人唾弃。"
    },
    {
      "location": "html，约翰福音21:3-6引文",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "They went forth, and entered into a ship immediately; and that night they caught nothing.",
      "suggested_fix": "改为“他们就出去，立刻上了船；那一夜他们什么也没有捕到。”",
      "translation_quote": "他们就出去，上了船，立时那夜什么也没有得。"
    },
    {
      "location": "html，耶稣问读者是否爱他的段落",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "“Defer to your brother”",
      "suggested_fix": "将“顺服弟兄”改为“谦让弟兄”，表达尊重、退让，而非无条件服从。",
      "translation_quote": "“顺服弟兄”"
    },
    {
      "location": "html，鼓励读者专注当下的段落",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "Peter walked with Jesus for three and a half years before he received this call from Jesus.",
      "suggested_fix": "将“才领受耶稣从他那里的这个呼召”改为“才领受耶稣的这个呼召”。",
      "translation_quote": "彼得与耶稣同行了三年半，才领受耶稣从他那里的这个呼召。"
    },
    {
      "location": "html，以人际关系解释爱的段落",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "We can best understand this in the context of human relationships.",
      "suggested_fix": "将“人人关系”改为“人际关系”。",
      "translation_quote": "我们可以在人人关系的语境中最好地理解这一点。"
    },
    {
      "location": "html，引用路加福音9:62的段落",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "<em>…No man, having put his hand to the plough, and looking back, is fit for the kingdom of God –Luke 9:62.</em>",
      "suggested_fix": "恢复引文原有的强调标签：<em>……手扶着犁向后看的，不配进神的国——路加福音 9:62。</em>",
      "translation_quote": "……手扶着犁向后看的，不配进神的国——路加福音 9:62。"
    },
    {
      "location": "html，描述耶稣走近岸边的段落",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "He is the friend of all and a stranger to none.",
      "suggested_fix": "将“他是众人的朋友，毫无陌生人”改为“他是众人的朋友，对谁都不陌生”。",
      "translation_quote": "他是众人的朋友，毫无陌生人。"
    }
  ],
  "findings_complete": true,
  "passed": false,
  "score": 90
}
